#X text 40 20 test_bufstats.pd -- isolates the one question left in the analysis chain: what shape does [fluid.bufstats] want its -stats buffer to be? Three declarations of the SAME destination \, identical in every other respect. Bang 1 \, 2 \, 3 \, then 4/5/6 in turn and read which of A/B/C prints DONE. Whichever one bangs is the declaration gnumbat-analyze.pd should use for stem_<x>_loud_stats., f 78;
#X text 40 225 2. run bufloudness. LOUD-DONE must print before anything below is meaningful.;
#X text 40 385 3. sanity check -- LOUDFEAT-FRAMES should be a large number. If it is 0 \, bufloudness wrote nothing and the bufstats question is moot., f 70;
#X text 40 555 4 / 5 / 6 -- the actual experiment. A = [array define name 14] (one array \, 14 points -- what gnumbat-analyze uses today \, and what fluid.bufstats-help.pd line 785 uses). B = [clone 14 fluid.multiarray] (14 arrays -- what "need 14" would imply if FluCoMa is counting statistics as CHANNELS). C = A again but with -numchans 1 pinning the source to one channel., f 78;
#X text 40 60 1. load a real stem into a plain mono array.;
